Your recursive Fibonacci is hitting a stack overflow because it lacks a terminating base case (e.g., if n <= 1: return n). Here is the fix and an iterative O(n) alternative to prevent deep recursion entirely:

def fib(n):
    if n <= 1:
        return n
    return fib(n - 1) + fib(n - 2)
